---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/SectionHead.astro';

const timeline = [
  { date: '2020–2023', text: 'Diploma in Mechanical Engineering, Gujarat Technological University. First Class with Distinction.' },
  { date: 'Sep 2023', text: 'Autodesk Certified User, AutoCAD.' },
  { date: 'Jan 2024', text: 'Certified SolidWorks Professional (CSWP), Mechanical Design.' },
  { date: 'Sep 2024', text: 'Started Engineering Design & Drafting Technology at Saskatchewan Polytechnic.' },
  { date: 'May–Aug 2025', text: 'Co-op term 1, Drafting Student, City of Saskatoon.' },
  { date: 'Jan–Aug 2026', text: 'Co-op terms 2 and 3, rehired for an 8-month term.' },
  { date: 'Mar–Jul 2026', text: 'Volunteer, Ganbatte Con, Saskatoon.' },
  { date: 'Apr 2027', text: 'Graduation (expected).' },
];
---
<Base
  title="About"
  description="About Manan Bhavsar: a mechanical engineering diploma, then drafting for the City of Saskatoon as an EDDT student at Saskatchewan Polytechnic."
>
  <section class="section wrap page-top">
    <SectionHead as="h1" title="Mechanical training, drafting across disciplines." />
    <p class="lede">
      I'm Manan Bhavsar, a drafting and design student at Saskatchewan Polytechnic. I grew up in Gujarat, India,
      came to Canada in 2023, and split my time between Moose Jaw for school and Saskatoon for co-op.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap about" aria-labelledby="story-title">
    <div class="about__story">
      <SectionHead title="How I got here" id="story-title" />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          After grade 10 I chose mechanical engineering, because I was curious about how machines work. I finished a Diploma in Mechanical Engineering at
          Gujarat Technological University with First Class with Distinction, and I topped the diploma's one
          CAD course. My final-year project was an electromagnetic braking system. After that I trained in
          3D CAD software at the Sopan Institute of Engineering &amp; Design in Ahmedabad.
        </p>
        <p>
          I wanted to study drafting properly, and I couldn't find the program I was looking for in India, so
          I looked at Canada. In April 2024 I chose Saskatchewan Polytechnic's EDDT program over two offers in
          Ontario. It teaches the software used across the industry: Revit for architectural, Civil 3D for civil
          and Inventor for mechanical. It's in Saskatchewan. And its paid co-op meant I could earn while I learn.
        </p>
        <p>
          Co-op with the City of Saskatoon is where the theory started to make sense. Drafting real water and
          sewer pipe drawings and road resurfacing plans to City standards connected what I had learned in
          class to real work.
        </p>
        <p>
          When a drafting task got repetitive, I started building small tools for it: AutoLISP routines and
          a Civil 3D plug-in. Some of them became part of the team's workflow, and some I kept for myself.
          The full story is on my <a href="/work/">co-op page</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          My class is the last EDDT cohort at Sask Polytech; the program closes after we graduate.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="about__timeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
      <h2 class="about__tl-title" id="timeline-title">Timeline</h2>
      <ol class="timeline">
        {timeline.map((t) => (
          <li>
            <span class="timeline__date">{t.date}</span>
            <span>{t.text}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap cols">
    <div>
      <SectionHead title="Outside drafting" id="outside-title" />
      <ul class="list">
        <li>
          <strong>Front End Supervisor (and cashier), Muhammad's No Frills, Moose Jaw.</strong>
          Part-time between co-op terms. They rehired me each time I came back.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Volunteer, Ganbatte Con</strong>, a non-profit anime convention in Saskatoon. I edited
          promotional videos for the social media team. At the convention I helped the front desk with
          registration and wristbands, ran cosplay prop and weapons checks, and set up vendor tables.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Volleyball.</strong> In India I organized an inter-college volleyball team and led it to a
          tournament win.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Languages:</strong> English, Hindi and Gujarati.</li>
        <li><strong>Also:</strong> Blender and video editing.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <SectionHead title="Certifications" id="certs-title" />
      <ul class="list">
        <li><strong>Certified SolidWorks Professional (CSWP)</strong>, Mechanical Design <span class="list__date num">Jan 2024</span></li>
        <li><strong>Autodesk Certified User</strong>, AutoCAD <span class="list__date num">Sep 2023</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted next">
        See my <a href="/resume/">resume</a>, or <a href="#contact">get in touch</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .about { display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); }
  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .about { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 320px; gap: var(--space-5); align-items: start; }
    .about__timeline { position: sticky; top: 100px; }
  }
  .about__timeline { border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); padding-top: var(--space-2); }

  .timeline { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: var(--space-2) 0 0; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .timeline li { position: relative; margin: 0; padding: 0 0 var(--space-2) var(--space-3); display: grid; gap: 0.15rem; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .timeline li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: -4px; top: 0.45em; width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); }
  .timeline__date { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--ink-3); }
  .about__tl-title { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0; margin: 0; }

  .cols { display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); }
  @media (min-width: 860px) { .cols { grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr; gap: var(--space-5); } }
  .list { padding: 0; list-style: none; max-width: var(--measure); }
  .list li { color: var(--ink-2); padding-block: 0.6rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin: 0; }
  .list strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .list__date { margin-left: 0.4rem; white-space: nowrap; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--ink-3); }
  .next { margin-top: var(--space-3); }
</style>
